# CODEOWNERS — vouchfx repository governance (S10-D-01)
# =============================================================================
# Purpose: require review on the surfaces where an unreviewed change does the
# most damage — the FROZEN v1 contracts (break every downstream consumer), the
# CI/release templates (a supply-chain surface), and the security/governance
# files themselves. GitHub auto-requests review from the listed owner(s) on any
# PR that touches a matching path, and — when the repo enables "Require review
# from Code Owners" branch protection — blocks merge until they approve.
#
# OWNER PLACEHOLDER
# -----------------
# `@tomas-rampas` is the sole owner TODAY because no GitHub org/teams exist yet.
# Once `vouchfx-org` (or equivalent) is created, SUBSTITUTE the individual for
# the appropriate teams, e.g.:
#     CI / release / supply-chain  -> @vouchfx-org/platform
#     security / disclosure        -> @vouchfx-org/security
#     frozen v1 contracts          -> @vouchfx-org/platform @vouchfx-org/security
# Team handles must be `@org/team` and the team must have write access to the
# repo, otherwise GitHub silently ignores the rule. GitHub can only fully
# validate owners against the real org — patterns here are syntactically valid
# but owner-resolution is unverifiable until the org/teams exist.
#
# PRECEDENCE: the LAST matching pattern wins (CODEOWNERS is last-match, unlike
# .gitignore). The catch-all is therefore first; the high-value paths follow and
# override it. Keep new high-value rules BELOW the catch-all.
# =============================================================================

# --- Catch-all: everything has an owner by default --------------------------
*                                               @tomas-rampas


# === Supply-chain surface: CI / CD / release templates ======================
# WHY: these workflows and templates execute in privileged CI with secrets/OIDC
# and define what downstream consumers run. A malicious or careless edit here is
# a software-supply-chain compromise (the core point of S10-D-01). Owner review
# is mandatory.
/.github/workflows/                             @tomas-rampas
/.github/actions/                               @tomas-rampas
/ci/                                            @tomas-rampas

# Central build / dependency-version / package-feed control. WHY: an unreviewed
# edit here silently changes a dependency version, adds a package source, or alters
# the build contract across the WHOLE solution — a classic supply-chain vector — so
# it must not be owned at the same bar as a README (it is otherwise catch-all only).
/Directory.Build.props                          @tomas-rampas
/Directory.Packages.props                       @tomas-rampas
/global.json                                    @tomas-rampas
/nuget.config                                   @tomas-rampas

# Memory-leak regression harness — the permanent Phase-1 (M1) CI gate (5,000-iteration
# provider-closure leak test, blocking in build.yml). WHY: weakening it (fewer
# iterations / a higher threshold) silently removes a hard-invariant safety gate.
/tests/Platform.Engine.Compilation.MemoryHarness/ @tomas-rampas


# === FROZEN v1 contracts — highest bar (Core-provider+ review) ==============
# WHY: these surfaces are frozen for the v1.x engine series and enforced by
# golden-file CI gates. A change here is, by definition, a breaking change to
# EVERY consumer (provider authors, the JSON Schema/IDE tooling, every event-
# stream renderer + the Healer agent). Evolution must be additive-only and
# deliberately reviewed — never an incidental diff.

# Provider SDK — the v1 interface contract (IStepProvider/IStepBinder/… and the
# CsxFragment composition rules). Frozen by SdkContractFreezeTests.
/src/Sdk/                                       @tomas-rampas

# Language JSON Schema source — the authored `.e2e.yaml` grammar. The composed
# schema is frozen; changing the source mutates what every author/IDE validates.
/src/Engine/Platform.Engine.Compilation/Schema/ @tomas-rampas

# Event-wire contract — top-level + nested value records of the JSON Lines event
# stream. Frozen by EventContractFreezeTests; any rename/type change breaks every
# renderer and the Healer.
/src/Engine/Platform.Engine.Abstractions/Events/ @tomas-rampas

# Golden files — the frozen baselines themselves (SDK contract, event contract,
# composed schema snapshots). These ARE the freeze; never edit without intent.
**/Golden/                                      @tomas-rampas
**/composed-schema.v1.json                      @tomas-rampas


# === Hard invariants + security/governance files ============================
# WHY: CLAUDE.md encodes the non-negotiable hard invariants (memory model,
# provider model, Aspire teardown, verdict taxonomy, secrets posture). SECURITY
# governs vulnerability disclosure. CODEOWNERS governs review itself. All three
# are governance surfaces that must not change without owner sign-off.
/CLAUDE.md                                       @tomas-rampas
/SECURITY.md                                     @tomas-rampas
/.github/CODEOWNERS                              @tomas-rampas
